{
  "duration": 67.019,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.1,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.719,
      "end": 3.079,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.659,
      "end": 8.859,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that the speeds of A and B are in the ratio of five is to six."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.42,
      "end": 10.219,
      "text": "Also, A takes"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.539,
      "end": 12.159,
      "text": "72 minutes to cover a fixed"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.539,
      "end": 13.019,
      "text": "distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.5,
      "end": 18.059,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how much time B will take to cover the same distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.359,
      "end": 22.5,
      "text": "Now let us assume the speed of A is 5X and the speed of B is 6X."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.879,
      "end": 24.319,
      "text": "Let us find the common distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.639,
      "end": 25.479,
      "text": "We know the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.879,
      "end": 27.579,
      "text": "distance is equal to speed into time."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.019,
      "end": 29.519,
      "text": "For A, distance is equal to"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.979,
      "end": 30.699,
      "text": "5X into"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.059,
      "end": 31.399,
      "text": "72."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.819,
      "end": 32.459,
      "text": "This gives us"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.819,
      "end": 34.059,
      "text": "360X."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.54,
      "end": 36.5,
      "text": "Since both of them cover the same distance,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.86,
      "end": 37.819,
      "text": "B also has to cover"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.139,
      "end": 39.359,
      "text": "360X."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.819,
      "end": 44.539,
      "text": "Now that we know the distance covered by B, let us find the time taken by B."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.2,
      "end": 51.939,
      "text": "Time taken by B is equal to distance covered by B, 360X, divided by the speed"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.299,
      "end": 52.779,
      "text": "6X."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.159,
      "end": 53.439,
      "text": "Here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.039,
      "end": 58.379,
      "text": "X gets canceled from both the numerator and the denominator."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.84,
      "end": 60.819,
      "text": "After simplifying this, we get 60 minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.34,
      "end": 64.439,
      "text": "So B takes 60 minutes to cover the same distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.939,
      "end": 67.019,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option B."
    }
  ],
